WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.433 --> 00:00:08.253
How can one cell swim, feed, control water, and reproduce without organs?

2
00:00:09.693 --> 00:00:12.513
In pond water, a Paramecium does all of them.

3
00:00:13.753 --> 00:00:15.153
Watch where each job happens.

4
00:00:16.217 --> 00:00:20.297
A unicellular organism is a living thing made of one cell.

5
00:00:21.497 --> 00:00:23.157
It has no tissues or organs.

6
00:00:24.577 --> 00:00:27.117
Its whole life must work inside one boundary.

7
00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:31.970
Bacteria, many algae, and many protists are unicellular.

8
00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:37.890
Each is a complete organism, not one cell broken away from a larger body.

9
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:40.800
Short cilia cover its surface.

10
00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:45.120
They beat together like oars, pushing the cell through water.

11
00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:48.480
Movement stays a job of this same cell.

12
00:00:49.483 --> 00:00:52.423
Food such as bacteria is swept into a groove.

13
00:00:53.623 --> 00:00:57.143
A food vacuole closes around it and travels through the cell.

14
00:00:58.563 --> 00:01:00.223
Digestion also happens inside.

15
00:01:01.317 --> 00:01:03.957
These jobs do not sit in separate organs.

16
00:01:05.257 --> 00:01:10.297
Moving, feeding, and digesting all occur within the membrane of one working cell.

17
00:01:11.350 --> 00:01:16.730
Pond water has fewer dissolved particles than the cell, so water keeps moving inward

18
00:01:16.730 --> 00:01:21.590
by osmosis. If that continued, what would the cell need to do?

19
00:01:28.017 --> 00:01:30.057
It must remove the extra water.

20
00:01:31.297 --> 00:01:35.897
Two contractile vacuoles, one toward each end, fill and squeeze water out.

21
00:01:37.077 --> 00:01:39.677
The cell stays intact as the cycle repeats.

22
00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:45.830
For reproduction, the Paramecium copies what it needs and pinches into two cells.

23
00:01:47.170 --> 00:01:51.330
One cell has carried movement, feeding, water control, and reproduction.

24
00:01:52.533 --> 00:01:55.713
Binary fission is reproduction without a partner.

25
00:01:56.973 --> 00:02:01.573
One cell divides into two, and each new cell must carry every life process.

26
00:02:02.717 --> 00:02:07.257
A multicellular organism can place major jobs in different cells.

27
00:02:08.537 --> 00:02:11.397
Those cells become specialized for particular work.

28
00:02:12.697 --> 00:02:14.877
Each cell's structure fits the job it does.

29
00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:18.880
Similar specialized cells can work as a tissue.

30
00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:22.120
Several tissues can build an organ.

31
00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:27.660
Related organs can form an organ system, all serving one organism.

32
00:02:28.833 --> 00:02:30.893
Muscle cells form muscle tissue.

33
00:02:32.533 --> 00:02:33.733
Several tissues form the heart.

34
00:02:34.913 --> 00:02:38.133
The heart works with blood vessels in the circulatory system.

35
00:02:39.167 --> 00:02:42.027
Sharing does not erase each cell's basic work.

36
00:02:43.267 --> 00:02:48.387
A muscle cell still takes in food molecules, makes ATP for energy, and maintains

37
00:02:48.387 --> 00:02:54.867
itself. Specialized means especially fitted for a job, not limited to only one job.

38
00:02:55.950 --> 00:02:57.630
The contrast is now clear.

39
00:02:58.930 --> 00:03:02.250
A Paramecium keeps every life process within one cell.

40
00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:08.390
A many-celled organism can share major jobs across cells shaped for their work.
